    "notes": "Current randomized study comparing FLASH and conventional proton radiotherapy for cats with oral squamous cell carcinoma, including tongue tumors. Radiation is given on three consecutive days at the Paul Scherrer Institute; cats remain hospitalized for four days at the University of Zurich Veterinary Hospital. Zurich handles enrollment and inpatient veterinary care; PSI is the radiation-delivery partner, not a separate owner-enrollment clinic. Initial CT and biopsy establish tumor extent/type; a temporary feeding tube is placed for treatment. Clinical follow-ups are weekly in month1 and every three months in year1, with CT at6,12,18 months. Final eligibility is confirmed by the study team."
  },
