    "notes": "Current randomized study comparing FLASH and conventional proton radiotherapy for cats with oral squamous cell carcinoma, including tongue tumors. Radiation is given on three consecutive days at the Paul Scherrer Institute; cats remain hospitalized for four days at the University of Zurich Veterinary Hospital. Zurich handles enrollment and inpatient veterinary care; PSI is the radiation-delivery partner, not a separate owner-enrollment clinic. Initial CT and biopsy establish tumor extent/type; a temporary feeding tube is placed for treatment. The May 2026 hospital flyer schedules weekly follow-up in the first month, then at months 2 and 3 and every three months during year one; CT is scheduled at 3, 6, 9 and 12 months after radiation. Final eligibility is confirmed by the study team."
